        "faq_1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Can you take calcium and iron together?",
            "a": "<p>It is best to take calcium and iron at different times of the day. Calcium can interfere with iron absorption when taken together in high doses. Space them a few hours apart to get the most benefit from each mineral.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Which form of magnesium is best?",
            "a": "<p>Different forms of magnesium serve different purposes. Magnesium citrate and glycinate are well absorbed and gentle on the stomach, supporting muscle relaxation and calm nerves, while oxide forms offer a higher concentrated mineral weight.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "q": "What are common signs you may be low in minerals?",
            "a": "<p>Low mineral levels can show up as persistent muscle cramps, fatigue, slow recovery, brittle nails, or frequent headaches. Because symptoms vary, consult your healthcare professional to test your levels before supplementing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "q": "How do minerals help with hydration?",
            "a": "<p>Electrolyte minerals such as sodium, potassium, and magnesium carry electrical charges that draw water into your cells. Water alone is not always enough; balance with key minerals keeps cellular hydration steady during exercise and heat.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "q": "Who should consider mineral supplementation?",
            "a": "<p>Active individuals, people on plant-based diets, pregnant women, and older adults often benefit from extra mineral support. Always check with your healthcare professional to identify your personal needs, especially before supplementing with iron.</p>"
          }
        }
