      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "Nutrient guide",
        "title": "Minerals",
        "lead": "<p>Minerals are essential elements from soil and water that your body needs but cannot make on its own. You must get them through food or supplements every day to keep your body working smoothly.</p><p>They play vital roles in your everyday health. Minerals build strong bones and teeth, help carry oxygen in your blood, and keep your muscles and nerves firing properly. They also support hormone balance and a healthy immune system.</p><p>Getting the right balance of minerals gives your body the foundation it needs for steady daily energy, recovery, and overall well-being.</p>",
        "hero_image": "shopify://shop_images/Velobiotics-Hero-minerals.png",
        "groups_title": "How minerals are grouped",
        "groups_intro": "<p>Minerals fall into two main categories based on daily amounts needed, plus key functional roles in electrolyte balance and nutrient competition.</p>",
        "nutrients_title": "Meet each mineral",
        "nutrients_intro": "<p>Explore the macro and trace minerals vital for your everyday health and wellness.</p>",
        "benefits_title": "What minerals do for you",
        "benefits": "<ul><li><strong>Bone &amp; teeth structure:</strong> Minerals like calcium and phosphorus build and maintain strong bones and teeth.</li><li><strong>Energy production:</strong> Iron, magnesium, and trace minerals help convert food into cellular energy.</li><li><strong>Nerve &amp; muscle function:</strong> Electrolytes such as sodium, potassium, and magnesium support nerve signals and muscle contractions.</li><li><strong>Immune defence &amp; cell repair:</strong> Zinc, copper, and selenium protect cells from oxidative stress and support immune function.</li><li><strong>Hormone &amp; enzyme balance:</strong> Iodine, chromium, and manganese assist thyroid hormone production and metabolic regulation.</li><li><strong>Fluid balance &amp; hydration:</strong> Key minerals keep cellular hydration and blood pressure levels steady.</li></ul>",
        "sources_title": "Natural food sources",
        "sources": "<p>You can find minerals across a variety of whole foods. Dairy, leafy greens, seeds, and nuts provide rich amounts of calcium and magnesium. Red meat, seafood, legumes, and dark poultry offer bioavailable iron and zinc. Whole grains, bananas, avocados, and root vegetables supply essential potassium and trace elements like manganese and selenium. Eating a balanced diet with diverse whole foods helps cover your daily mineral intake.</p>",
        "why_title": "Why supplement?",
        "why": "<p>Modern diets and environmental factors can make it challenging to obtain optimal mineral levels solely from food:</p><ul><li><strong>Depleted agricultural soils:</strong> Intensive farming methods often reduce the mineral content of crops and produce.</li><li><strong>Processed food consumption:</strong> Refining whole foods strips away key natural minerals and fiber.</li><li><strong>Increased losses:</strong> Intense exercise, sweating, heavy periods, or pregnancy increase your daily need for specific minerals like iron and electrolytes. Always check with your healthcare professional before taking iron supplements, and note iron only when a need is confirmed.</li><li><strong>Plant-based diets:</strong> Plant foods may contain phytates that reduce mineral bioavailability, requiring careful planning.</li><li><strong>Ageing &amp; bone density:</strong> As we age, mineral absorption decreases, making calcium and magnesium support more important.</li></ul><p>Always check with your healthcare professional before starting new supplements.</p>",
        "syn_title": "Why probiotics make them work better",
        "syn_text": "Velobiotics pairs essential minerals with micro-shielded probiotics to support optimal absorption. Healthy gut bacteria ferment dietary fibers to produce short-chain fatty acids, which lower intestinal pH and make minerals like calcium, magnesium, and iron easier to dissolve. By protecting the gut lining and maintaining a balanced microbiome, live probiotics help your digestive tract absorb minerals more efficiently. Our unique micro-shielding technology shields each individual bacterium so they arrive active where you need them most.",
        "syn_link": "Learn about micro-shielded probiotics",
        "syn_url": "/pages/science-technology",
        "faq_title": "Common questions",
        "products_title": "Shop minerals range",
        "products_intro": "<p>Discover Velo16 Calcium &amp; Magnesium in this collection, featuring essential minerals combined with 16 live probiotic strains. Also explore our targeted <a href=\"/collections/magnesium\">magnesium</a>, <a href=\"/collections/iron\">iron</a>, and <a href=\"/collections/zinc\">zinc</a> products via nutrient cards above.</p>",
        "disclaimer": "Supplements support a healthy diet and lifestyle. They do not treat, cure or prevent any disease. Speak to your healthcare professional if you are pregnant, breastfeeding, on medication or have a medical condition."
      }
